p.src:
The first route is the one Sandel rejects: $\begin{aligned}
\text{relativist justice}
&=
\text{fidelity to the shared understandings of a tradition},\\
\text{relativist justice}
&\Longrightarrow
\text{justice as creature of convention}.\end{aligned}$ If this were all that it meant to tie justice to the good, the segregationist objection would be fatal. Justice would lose its critical character and become a mere echo of local circumstance.

