One conception is the familiar liberal one: $\text{respect}_{\mathrm{liberal}}
=
\text{bracketing or abstracting from moral and religious convictions}.$ On this view, we respect our fellow citizens by setting their deeper moral and religious commitments aside for political purposes. We do not deny those commitments; we simply refrain from bringing them into public argument.

