p.src:
The final conclusion is therefore not a final verdict on one controversy. It is a more general civic claim: $\text{politics of moral engagement}
\Longrightarrow
\text{better appreciation of plural human goods}.$ To the extent that our moral and religious disagreements reflect an irreducible plurality of human goods, a politics of moral engagement is better suited than a politics of bracketing to appreciating what different forms of life express.

